    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0777" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v09/pg751"/>

                <head>335. National Security Action Memorandum No. 4<anchor n="0" xml:id="d335-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-02-04">February 4,
                        1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list type="to">
                    <head>TO</head>
                    <item>The Secretary of Defense</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Purchases of Uranium from Foreign Countries</item>
                </list>
                <p>In the light of discussion at the National Security Council on February 1,
                        1961,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d335-f2"/> the President requested the Secretary
                    of Defense to consult with the Atomic Energy Commission about a review of the
                    purchases of uranium from foreign countries. It is accordingly requested that
                    this review be undertaken and that this office be informed whether, in fact,
                    there is any hope of early savings of foreign exchange in this area.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">McGeorge
                                Bundy</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d335-f3"
                    /></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
